## What moved, read in the source

A judge was given call and target only, shuffled, and not told which side of the comparison a pair came from (one seed; 15 call sites per row unless a count is given).

| | Java | Kotlin | PHP |
|---|---|---|---|
| lost: right before | 4 of 15 | 9 of 15 | 8 of 15 |
| different target: wrong before, right now | 15 of 15 | 9 of 15 | 15 of 15 |
| different target: right before, wrong now | 0 | 3 | 0 |
| gained: right | 15 of 15 | 13 of 15 | 15 of 15 |

Also: Java binds through a static import 8 right of 10; Java constructions retargeted 10 of 10 wrong before and right now, new ones 10 of 10 right; Kotlin name-step binds on calls nothing resolved before 14 of 15; Kotlin `class_hint` binds on such calls 14 of 15; PHP new constructions 9 of 10; PHP lost constructions 5 of 5 wrong before. Each adapter also read its own samples before the shared changes; those readings are in the notebook reports.

The three Kotlin edges that went from right to wrong, and most of the wrong gained ones, are overloads: the linker's method index keeps the last overload of a name (255 Kotlin edges changed overload). That gap is on file with these numbers and is the next change planned, before batch 5b.

## The languages already moved did not move

Six C# repositories, two Rust and one TypeScript are edge-for-edge identical to dev. On knex two recovery edges keep caller and target and change line.

## Not done, each on file with its count

Overload selection by argument count in the shared layer; stubs of one name from one caller collapsing before the linkers run (432 Kotlin stubs lose facts; 5 of the 9 right Kotlin losses); the return type of a callee typing a later receiver; a receiver that is a call result (why the name step is off for PHP); PHP traits as ancestors; one qualified name declared in two files (168 binds on grpc's generated PHP copies); inherited member types, a Kotlin function beside a class of its name, `pkg.f()`; an unresolved `instantiates` stub carries confidence 0.95, the resolved value of `new` (giving that pathway an unresolved value also raises the floor of every graded resolved construction in every language, so it was taken back out of this branch).

## What must not change

Measured on the seven repositories against dev. Symbols (ids, names, qualified names, stable ids): identical. Edges other than `calls` and `instantiates`: identical on koel, grpc, spring-petclinic and detekt-core. On jedis and commons-compress `uses` edges move (jedis 242 gone, 32 new; commons-compress 22 gone, 128 new): the inherited-calls linker makes them beside a call bind, and the ones read are the `Builder` binds to a parent package that are gone. On okhttp `extends` 13 gone and 4 new, `implements` 16 gone and 26 new (this branch keeps a supertype written `Outer.Nested` whole; it was cut to `Outer`), and `dispatches_to` 11 gone and 122 new, derived from them. Ranked entrypoint lists change with the call graph: jedis 277 to 285 entries, commons-compress 154 to 161, koel 191 to 197, detekt-core 0 to 1; `request_ingress` keeps its count on every tree.

## Not checked

No repository outside the seven (and the ten of the earlier languages) was run. Confidence values of moved edges, and the effect of the moved edges on slice, dead-code and taint output beyond the existing tests, were not compared. Which entries entered and left the ranked entrypoint lists was not read.
